From 08a16bb1894e90c51d23e09887e5c677315e0a65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:56:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] ASoC: ak4961: port arrays per stream (speakers were
 silent), microphone 1

- The SLIMbus controller runtime-suspends between streams and the bus
  restarts, which clears the PGD port arrays written at bring-up: the
  SLIMbus RX data never reached SBI1 and the speakers stayed silent
  although the amplifiers ran. Write them in every hw_params, after
  refreshing the interface device's logical address, as ZTE does.
- AIF1 capture (ak4961_tx1) on SLIM TX7/TX8 (PGD ports 6/7): ZTE's
  handset-mic path without the DSP (AIN1 with MPWR1A bias, MIC amp 1L,
  ADC1L, SBO1L = ADC1), charge pump 1 and mic bias timing from ZTE's
  events; controls MIC Gain 1L, CP1 Clock Mode, Mic_1L input and SBO1L
  source.

DT: Microphone link (SLIMBUS_0_TX), MultiMedia2 front end (playback and
capture at the same time), earpiece switch (PM8994 GPIO 13) on the
first TFA9890.

Tested: SBI1 looped to SBO1L returns the played tone bit-exact; speaker
to microphone: a -21 dBFS 1 kHz tone saturates the microphone at 21 dB
gain; the vibrator raises the microphone level by about 30 dB.

